remains low at around 4.1 percent, and both job openings and weekly hours have been

increasing. Unemployment claims, on a four-week moving average, are running at levels

consistent with full employment. So, the labor side of the Fed’s congressional remit is in good

shape.

         Yet for more than five years, inflation has been running above target. So, our

predominant focus is on the price-stability side of our mandate. The plain fact is that inflation is

