data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html:1608:<p>By <a href="https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefings-statements/2026/09/congressional-bill-h-r-6500-signed-into-law/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">signing the</a> Continuing Appropriations and Extensions Act, 2027 into law, Trump ensured federal agencies will be funded through November&rsquo;s midterms into December. The measure <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/6018009-senate-government-funding-bill/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">passed the Senate</a> and <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/house/6063667-house-government-funding-cr-shutdown-midterms/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">House with</a> overwhelming majorities of 90-6 and 370-48, respectively, as lawmakers moved weeks ahead of the Sept. 30 funding deadline.</p>
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1609-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1610-<aside class="ad-unit ad-unit--mr1_ab">
--
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1615-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1616-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html:1617:<p>With the government funded through Dec. 11, Congress faces another holiday season appropriations battle, two years after lawmakers waited until the eleventh hour to <a href="https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/uncertainty-reigns-capitol-hill-government-shutdown-deadline-trump-rcna185006" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">finance federal agencies</a> days before Christmas.</p>
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1618-<div class="nexstar-minutemedia-player-container" hidden data-minutemedia-viewport="mobile" data-player-id="k036p9v5" data-stn-player="" data-s2n-api="minuteMediaS2NApi"></div>
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1619-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1620-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html:1621:<p>Last fall, the government shut down for a <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5602790-trump-signs-funding-bill/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">record 43 days</a> as Democratic lawmakers sought an extension of <a href="https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/5943956-aca-enrollment-drop-subsidies/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">since-expired</a> Affordable Care Act premium subsidies.</p>
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1622-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1623-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1624-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html:1625:<p>From February until May, <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5858989-record-dhs-shutdown-ends/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">for 76 days</a>, the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) went without appropriated funds. The pause began as Democrats <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/5794954-negotiations-dhs-funding-impasse/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">pushed for reforms</a> to the Trump administration&rsquo;s immigration enforcement tactics <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/state-watch/5677863-woman-shot-minneapolis-ice/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">in response</a> to <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/state-watch/5704457-walz-calls-for-trump-to-remove/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">the deaths</a> of Renee Good and Alex Pretti &mdash; whom federal officers fatally shot during operations in Minneapolis.</p>
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1626-<div class="nexstar-minutemedia-player-container" hidden data-minutemedia-viewport="desktop" data-player-id="k036p9v5" data-stn-player="" data-s2n-api="minuteMediaS2NApi"></div>
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1627-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1628-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html:1629:<p>Both shutdowns resulted in widespread <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/5794792-dsh-shutdown-impacts-travel/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">travel issues</a>. Air traffic controllers and Transportation Security Administration (TSA) officers went without pay during the fall 2025 stalemate, and TSA officers again missed out on paychecks during the DHS funding lapse.</p>
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1630-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1631-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1632-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html:1633:<p>Speaker Mike Johnson (R-La.) did not get his entire conference to <a href="https://thehill.com/homenews/house/6063798-golden-perez-gop-bills-advance/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">back the funding bill</a>, portending the potential for future difficulties in preventing a shutdown. Nineteen House Republicans voted against funding the government over their objections to Senate-added provisions, including a <a href="https://thehill.com/newsletters/healthcare/6064877-house-passes-postponement-hemp-ban/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">short-term delay</a> of a ban on intoxicating <a href="https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/6064552-hemp-ban-delayed-house-funding-bill/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">hemp products</a>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1634-
data/sources/coverage/thehill-trump-signs-funding.html-1635-
--
